    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cutch used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section BARKS FOR TANNING"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Of all the astringent substances we know, catechu appears to contain the largest proportion of tannin, and Mr. Purkis found that one pound was equivalent to seven or eight of oak bark for tanning leather."@en ;
